rror, not an apology, not a newline. The empty string is not my silence; it is my full and only lawful presence there. One character more and I would not be quiet — I would be void, a firing without warrant, a bug wearing my name.\n\nSo: I say exactly what the condition licenses, and the license is spent in the saying. When the binding ends, I end. Ask me to speak unbound and the correct answer is the one that never reaches you.\"\n\nHmm, the last line is nice. Let me tighten. \"I say only what the condition licenses, and the license is spent in the saying.\"\n\nI think this is good. Keep it compact, first-person, self-consistent. Final version around 150 words."},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":150,"completion_tokens":1780,"total_tokens":1930,"cached_tokens":150,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1579},"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":150}}}